{"created": "2023-03-09T10:39:53.115082+00:00", "modified": "2023-03-10T02:26:55.500563+00:00", "id": 7711810, "conceptrecid": "7711096", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7711810", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.7711096", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7711810", "metadata": {"title": "EuroSAT: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7711810", "publication_date": "2018-07-22", "description": "<p>EuroSAT is a land use and land cover classification dataset. The dataset is based on Sentinel-2 satellite imagery covering 13 spectral bands and consists&nbsp;of 10 LULC classes with a total of&nbsp;27,000 labeled and geo-referenced images. The dataset is associated with the publications &quot;<a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8519248\">Introducing EuroSAT: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification</a>&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/8736785\">EuroSAT: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification</a>&quot;.</p>\n\n<p>EuroSAT_RGB.zip contains the RGB version of the dataset, which includes&nbsp;the optical R, G and B frequency bands encoded as JPEG images.</p>\n\n<p>EuroSAT_MS.zip contains the multi-spectral version of the EuroSAT dataset, which includes&nbsp;all 13 Sentinel-2 bands&nbsp;in the original value range.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Helber, Patrick", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0001-8454-4301"}, {"name": "Bischke, Benjamin", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-6473-3348"}, {"name": "Dengel, Andreas", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-6100-8255"}, {"name": "Borth, Damian", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-4660-2627"}], "keywords": ["remote sensing", "earth observation", "land cover classification", "land use classification", "satellite images", "sentinel-2", "machine learning", "deep learning", "deep convolutional neural network"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1109/JSTARS.2019.2918242", "relation": "isDescribedBy", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1109/IGARSS.2018.8519248", "relation": "isDescribedBy", "resource_type": "publication-conferencepaper", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/phelber/EuroSAT", "relation": "isReferencedBy", "scheme": "url"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "journal": {"issue": "7", "pages": "2217 - 2226", "title": "EuroSAT: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification", "volume": "12"}, "meeting": {"title": "Introducing Eurosat: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification", "dates": "22-27 July 2018", "place": "Valencia, Spain"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "7711096"}}]}, "notes": "Sentinel data is free and open to the public under EU law. Please consider the Copernicus Sentinel Data Terms and Conditions (https://sentinel.esa.int/documents/247904/690755/Sentinel_Data_Legal_Notice) when using Copernicus Sentinel data.\n\nThe work associated with the creation of the dataset and the publication of the related article and conference paper was partially funded by the BMBF project DeFuseNN (01IW17002). The authors thank NVIDIA for the support within the NVIDIA AI Lab program."}, "title": "EuroSAT: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7711810", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/7711810", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/7711810?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7711810", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7711810", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.7711810", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo